lines=['# One-bin y2 control: exact return to the original capped suffix','', '**Candidate; execution-owner verification complete, independent lead acceptance pending.** The single authorized cell completed and all owned jobs ended. No control GPU rerun or follow-up arm was executed.','', '## Decision','', 'Changing only supplied row137 y2 from999 to998 is insufficient at this frozen477415/R16 history. The entire1851-token FREE suffix is token-for-token identical to accepted C00. Its first row immediately restores chair [0,999,999,999], repeats that box for205 complete free rows, and ends at the3084 total-token cap with one incomplete fragment. There is no new known-owner coverage, no first nonzero-x1 and no excursion into the later all999 regime.','', 'This is a technically valid negative for THIS edit, not an execution failure and not proof of a semantic mechanism. It cannot overturn the category-only counterexample: C10 already recovered owners while its supplied box remained invalid.','', '## Matched outcome and credit','', '| Cell | Common136 + free coverage | Free-only coverage | G/L vs common136 | Free complete invalid | Malformed fragments | Valid-box strict repeats | Free tokens / stop |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|','| C00, reused |2/27|0|0/0|205|1|0|1851 / cap|','| Y998, new |2/27|0|0/0|205|1|0|1851 / cap|','| C01, reused positive |18/27|16|16/0|160|1|15|1851 / cap|','', 'C10/C11 remain descriptive positive references: both recover the same16 as C01 and also relapse/cap. Y998 recovers NONE of those16; all16 are missing from its recovered set, with no replacement gains. All common-history matches are retained with no assignment swaps. Free owner identities are empty; complete per-owner comparisons and the16 missing IDs are in result.json.','', 'Supplied137 is excluded from matching and free-error counts. Free valid predictions and annotation-unmatched UNKNOWN predictions are both0 in Y998. Zero strict valid-box repeats does not mean good behavior: every complete free box is invalid. Counts with and without supplied-history duplicate references both remain0. Common history and supplied137 are not presented as recovered free owners.','', '## Intervention fidelity and inference limits','', 'The only full-target token difference from C00 is action offset1231: token152669→152668, verified by the actual tokenizer as coord_999→coord_998. The unchanged prefix contains1224 tokens, the supplied row is nine tokens, and its mask ends exactly at1233. All later logits, including opener and EOS choices, remain unrestricted. No prefix row was dropped or reserialized.','', 'This history change was consumed: at the next category decision the chair top1–runner-up logit margin changes from0.184498 in C00 to0.140511 in Y998, while chair remains top. The next x1=0 margin changes1.216604→1.207817. Thus identical greedy output is not evidence that the token edit was ignored. These local margins are supporting evidence, not an embedding norm or full-distribution comparison.','', 'One bin numerically need not be a small embedding-vector or probability perturbation. The box changes zero-height→inverted-height, not identical geometry semantics; no norm matching was performed. Failure establishes only this edit’s insufficiency. Success of other edits and failure here do not imply arbitrary changes work, validity is globally necessary, or coordinate embeddings are defective.','', '## Strongest surviving explanations, ranked','', '1. **Best supported:** this repeated trajectory tolerates this particular recent y2 edit at the greedy-decision level and immediately returns to its original suffix, whereas the accepted category and large y1 changes access a different transient enumeration route. Escape depends on the specific history change.', '2. **Live alternatives:** slot/direction sensitivity and the extent/validity effects of C01 remain confounded. A one-bin y2 failure does not explain why a large y1 edit succeeds; category-only success shows validity restoration is not a universal prerequisite.', '3. **Unresolved:** a learned endpoint/embedding/readout prior, visual grounding state or cached-history copying could contribute, but none is identified by this single control. No KV/embedding intervention or vector-norm comparison was performed.','', '## ONE next discriminator — proposed, not executed','', 'Propose one matched valid near-boundary row: chair [0,998,999,999], changing the SAME token pair999→998 at y1 rather than y2. Reuse bound C00, Y998 and C01 outputs if all runtime/source bindings remain exact. This is one new cell, not a sweep.','', 'If it recovers free owners while Y998 does not, full-image extent is unnecessary and a slot/validity-dependent distinction becomes more plausible. It would NOT isolate validity alone because the token position also changes. If both near-boundary edits fail while C01 succeeds, larger extent/direction/history effects remain live; numerical distance still is not embedding distance. Judge full free-owner identities, relapse, invalid/malformed/repeat burden and EOS jointly, with supplied137 excluded. Lead decides whether this contrast is worth running; no next phase was launched.','', '## Technical checks, cost and reproducibility','', 'Accepted C00/C01 (and descriptive C10/C11) panel/config/checkpoint/embeddings/native settings/receipts/raw outputs/consumer were hash-bound and reused without GPU execution. Loaded-model descriptor, actual bs4 order/padding, generation settings, prompt-position digest and cache-seam metadata exactly match C00. Natural pre-intervention argmax checks passed; the original first136 target rows and all three companion sequences/stops are exact.','', 'Independent reduction invokes the exact accepted consume function without changing its globals or implementation. The same credit-exclusion sensitivity fixture passes: a synthetic full-image owner matches1 if the supplied row is admitted and0 if excluded; the scientific bank is unchanged. The derivative producer snapshot/diff changes only output root, inherited C00 path, single-arm CLI choice and description. No model-execution logic changed.','', f"Cost: {d['technical']['counts']['model_forwards']} native bs4 forward invocations ({4*d['technical']['counts']['model_forwards']} batch slots including finished-companion padding),1 vision invocation,1851 target free tokens; {d['technical']['elapsed_gpu_seconds']:.2f} allocated GPU-seconds ({d['technical']['elapsed_gpu_seconds']/3600:.4f} GPU-hours). One successful attempt, no control rerun; exit0. The5000-call ceiling was respected. Wall time includes loading/checks rather than measuring GPU kernel time.",'', f'- [Frozen panel]({R}/panel.json): checkpoint/config/model/bank bindings, exact histories and inherited controls.',f'- [Independent result]({R}/result.json), SHA256 `{bind(R/"result.json")["sha256"]}`.',f'- [Raw output]({R}/runtime/Y998/raw.json), [runtime receipt]({R}/runtime/Y998/receipt.json), [exact edit/mask receipt]({R}/edit-receipt.json).',f'- [Executed derivative]({R}/producer.py), [explicit source diff]({R}/producer.diff), [independent consumer entry]({R}/reduce.py), [launch command]({R}/run.sh).',f'- [Candidate terminal receipt]({R}/terminal.json) and [accepted factorial](../2026-09-16-corner-loop-bridge-factorial/results.md).','', 'The target is stable for lead acceptance. Accepted predecessor result.json/terminal.json/scripts/state were not rewritten. No live owned jobs, training, labels, extra images, embedding/KV changes or further experiment.','']
